        <title type="html"><![CDATA[identitycredential.providers.nonce is deprecated and removed from the…]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28684</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28684"/>
        <updated>2025-12-17T01:56:39.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/432915?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">The <code class="notranslate">nonce</code> property of <a href="https://w3c-fedid.github.io/FedCM/#dictdef-identityproviderrequestoptions" rel="nofollow">IdentityProviderRequestOptions</a> has been deprecated and removed from the spec:</p>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://w3c-fedid.github.io/FedCM/#dictdef-identityproviderrequestoptions" rel="nofollow">https://w3c-fedid.github.io/FedCM/#dictdef-identityproviderrequestoptions</a><br>
<a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2518008808" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/w3c-fedid/custom-requests/issues/3" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/w3c-fedid/custom-requests/issues/3/hovercard" href="https://github.com/w3c-fedid/custom-requests/issues/3">w3c-fedid/custom-requests#3</a><br>
<a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3283416319" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/w3c-fedid/FedCM/issues/768" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/w3c-fedid/FedCM/pull/768/hovercard" href="https://github.com/w3c-fedid/FedCM/pull/768">w3c-fedid/FedCM#768</a></p>
<p dir="auto">It didn't already exist as a subfeature so I added it. I guessed about browser version: I set it to the first version to support identity credentials at all, based on:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>It didn't already have a subfeature, so I assume it was already supported when <code class="notranslate">IdentityProviderRequestOptions</code> was initially supported.</li>
<li>You can't really do identity credentials at all without some version of <code class="notranslate">IdentityProviderRequestOptions</code> (not necessarily <code class="notranslate">nonce</code>, but definitely <code class="notranslate">clientId</code> and <code class="notranslate">configURL</code>.</li>
</ul>]]></content>
