<p dir="auto"><a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3125441720" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27003" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27003/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27003">#27003</a> by <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/Elchi3/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/Elchi3">@Elchi3</a> ran the BCD Collector for Chrome 135 beta but it seems to have set the Android support to false for any new entries but I see no reason for this.</p>
<p dir="auto">Some of these have been corrected manually (e.g. in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3125441720" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27003" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27003/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27003">#27003</a>) but these have not.</p>
<p dir="auto"><a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/Elchi3/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/Elchi3">@Elchi3</a> do you know why this was? Should I raise an issue for this? I don't see the same for the latest Chrome 144 beta nor, 134/136 either side of this bad one. So maybe a one off issue?</p>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>

<p dir="auto">To be honest I have not tested these all, but I see no reason they were set to unsupported since, unless there is an exceptional reason, most changes to Chrome are also supported in Chrome Android and there are no reasons for these.</p>

